From bb6ee31723466690d70a951cb38a6451410152db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hc-push <hc-push@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:50:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: opt-in SystemSignal::OpsIntegrated

Notify app websocket connections that opt in (AppRequest::SubscribeOpsIntegrated)
when DHT ops held by this conductor are committed as integrated. An observer on
DhtStore, shared by all clones of a DNA's store, covers both the integration
workflow and self-authored ops written as integrated by SourceChain::flush.

Delivery never blocks integration: a single atomic check when nobody
subscribed; otherwise batches go to a bounded queue (try_send, dropped and
counted when full) drained by one task, which preserves batch order and splits
batches into signals of at most 500 ops. Connections that did not opt in never
receive the variant (holochain_client 0.9.x cannot decode unknown signals).
Signals are best effort; DumpOpTimings remains the reconciliation path.
